<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Metadata for the pull widget, read by the launcher before any of our code runs.

  ## Sizes

  The same square as the recently added card — 166dp on design/html/15-Widget.html,
  200dp on design/html/18-TabletWidget.html, one fluid composition at both — so
  the cell counts and the minima match it deliberately. Two cards drawn side by
  side on the same artboard that snapped to different cell sizes would not sit
  level on a real home screen.

  The one difference is the vertical floor. This card has no artwork, so its
  content is a 22dp glyph, a 36sp number, a title line and a 4dp bar:

    * minWidth 140dp — the 36sp percentage and the album title are both single
      lines, and 140dp is where a title stops being a word.
    * minHeight 140dp — glyph, number, title and bar with 28dp of padding. Below
      WidgetSquareDimensions.barMinHeight (120dp) the bar drops, because it is
      the only thing on the card the percentage above it already says.
    * maxResizeHeight is 320dp for the same reason as the other square: there is
      nothing here that grows.

  ## updatePeriodMillis is 0, deliberately

  Twice deliberately, on this card. The platform's own period is clamped to 30
  minutes and wakes the device, and REQUIREMENTS.md "Polling schedule" already
  has a background poller checking the activity summary on a schedule designed
  around battery — so a widget period would be a second, worse poller running
  beside the good one, and the numbers it drew would be no fresher. While the
  process is alive the Glance session recomposes from the mirrored pull table as
  polls write to it; when it is not, the redraw is pushed by
  NeedlerWidgets.refreshPulls when the summary's revision moves. See PullWidget's
  KDoc.

  ## previewLayout

  widget_pull_preview.xml, which draws the resting card — an em dash, "Nothing
  pulling" and an empty track, in the muted grey rather than the positive green.
  That is the honest preview: it is what the card shows nearly all the time, and
  a picker promising "62%" would be advertising a pull the user has not placed.
-->
<appwidget-provider xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:description="@string/widget_pulls_description"
    android:initialLayout="@layout/glance_default_loading_layout"
    android:minWidth="140dp"
    android:minHeight="140dp"
    android:minResizeWidth="110dp"
    android:minResizeHeight="110dp"
    android:maxResizeWidth="320dp"
    android:maxResizeHeight="320dp"
    android:previewLayout="@layout/widget_pull_preview"
    android:resizeMode="horizontal|vertical"
    android:targetCellWidth="2"
    android:targetCellHeight="2"
    android:updatePeriodMillis="0"
    android:widgetCategory="home_screen" />
